--TEST--
An enum case `Core\Cache` stores reads back as a case, on the per-core and the process tier, so `is` still names its enum and a case backed by `0` stays truthy — `rule:enums/representation` and `rule:core-api/two-cache-tiers`
--FILE--
<?nvs
enum Mode: int {
    A = 0,
    B = 1,
}

array<Mode> $modes = [Mode::A, Mode::B];
foreach ([Core\Cache::local(), Core\Cache::process()] as var $cache) {
    $cache->put("modes", $modes);
    var $back = $cache->get("modes") as array<mixed>;
    mixed $first = Core\Arr::first($back);
    echo "is Mode=", $first is Mode ? "true" : "false";
    echo " truthy=", $first ? "true" : "false", "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
is Mode=true truthy=true
is Mode=true truthy=true
